# graphify scope control — keep the knowledge graph limited to the source that
# matters (crates/, apps/, design/) so full rebuilds (post-checkout hook,
# `graphify update`) don't silently expand to the whole repo.
#
# Whitelist form (gitignore syntax, as documented in the graphify README):
# ignore everything, then re-include only the three source trees. This is
# self-maintaining — any new top-level folder is excluded by default, and it
# does not depend on the root .gitignore (which graphify shadows once a
# .graphifyignore exists in the same directory).
#
# Build/VCS noise (target/, node_modules/, dist/, .git/) is also handled by
# graphify's built-in skip list, independent of these rules.

*

!crates/
!crates/**
!apps/
!apps/**
!design/
!design/**
